 [:db/cas 17592186259863 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨1,\\,x⟩$ and the points $A(1,0)$ and $B(e,1)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2(e-1),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2(e-1),$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the segment line $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n- $F$ is conservative." "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨1,\\,x⟩$ and the points $A(1,0)$ and $B(e,1)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2(e-1),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2(e-1),$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the segment line $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n\n- **IV.** $F$ is conservative."]
